#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:62
msgid ""
"// Create a file with a raw syscall with write-only and create permissions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:63
msgid "\"c_str.txt\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:64
msgid ""
"// Pass the ownership of an integer file descriptor to an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `OwnedFd::drop()` closes the file descriptor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:67
msgid "\"Could not open file with syscall!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:69
msgid ""
"// Create a `BorrowedFd` from an `OwnedFd`.\n"
"    // `BorrowedFd::drop()` does not close the file because it doesn't own "
"it!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:72
msgid "// std::mem::drop(owned_fd); // ❌🔨\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:75
msgid "// owned_fd will be dropped here, and the file will be closed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:81
msgid "A file descriptor represents a specific process's access to a file."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:83
msgid ""
"Reminder: Device and OS-specific features are exposed as if they were files "
"on unix-style systems."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:86
msgid ""
"[`OwnedFd`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3128-io-safety.html#ownedfd-and-"
"borrowedfdfd) is an owned wrapper type for a file descriptor. It _owns_ the "
"file descriptor, and closes it when dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:90
msgid ""
"Note: We have our own implementation of it here, draw attention to the "
"explicit `Drop` implementation."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:93
msgid ""
"`BorrowedFd` is its borrowed counterpart, it does not need to close the file "
"when it is dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:96
msgid "Note: We have not explicitly implemented `Drop` for `BorrowedFd`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:98
msgid ""
"`BorrowedFd` uses a lifetime captured with a `PhantomData` to enforce the "
"invariant \"if this file descriptor exists, the OS file descriptor is still "
"open even though it is not responsible for closing that file descriptor.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:102
msgid ""
"The lifetime parameter of `BorrowedFd` demands that there exists another "
"value in your program that lasts as long as that specific `BorrowedFd` or "
"outlives it (in this case an `OwnedFd`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:106
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Uncomment the `std::mem::drop(owned_fd)` line and try to "
"compile to show that `borrowed_fd` relies on the lifetime of `owned_fd`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:109
msgid ""
"This has been encoded by the API designers to mean _that other value is what "
"keeps the access to the file open_."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md:112
msgid ""
"Because Rust's borrow checker enforces this relationship where one value "
"must last at least as long as another, users of this API do not need to "
"worry about handling this correct file descriptor aliasing and closing logic "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
